A frontend block schema with no fieldsets keeps the default fieldset Inka gives it, however many times the frontend sends INIT. The default was added for new block types only, so a frontend that sent INIT twice (a client-side hydration) had its second, unfilled copy merged over the first, and the editor crashed on load ("Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'map')") on a page holding such a block with a field left empty. A schema that still reaches the container-child enhancer without fieldsets now fails with an error naming the block.
